<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Verulamium</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Verlamion</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Verulamium was a Roman town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> beside modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-albans">St Albans</a>, grown from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> settlement of Verlamion, a centre of the Catuvellauni. It became a self-governing municipium, was sacked by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boudica">Boudica</a>'s rebels in 60 or 61, and was rebuilt with a forum and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>. Saint Alban, Britain's first recorded Christian martyr, was executed there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/verulamium.jpg" alt="Verulamium" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gary Houston · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20050410-009-verulamium-wall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
